          //  Other  Patch  Relations

                Pitch Operator  (  As Pitch Operator  )    n  -->  1    Pitch  (  Pitch  )

//  Attributes

      //  General  Classes'  Attributes

            Workspace  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Pitch  -->  Hertz  (  Double  )      //  Should  become  derived  :  Hertz  =  Base Hertz  *  Factor
            Pitch  -->  Base Hertz  (  Double  )
            Pitch  -->  Factor  (  Double  )

            Document  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Curve  -->  Name  (  String  )
            Curve  -->  Time  (  Double  )  //  Would  have  been  a  parameter  of  the  Value  method.
            Curve  -->  Value  (  Double  )  //  Would  have  a  method  if  a  method  could  have  a  return  value.

            Node  -->  Time  (  Double )
            Node  -->  Value  (  Double )
            Node  -->  Type  (  Integer  )      //  Should  become  enum  Node Types  instead  of  Integer
            Node  -->  Direction  (  Double  )

            Dimensioner  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Analyser  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Sample  -->  Name  (  String  )
            Sample  -->  File Path  (  String  )
            Sample  -->  Loaded  (  Boolean  )      //  Write  access  should  become  private
            Sample  -->  Mono / Stereo  (  Integer  )      //  Should  become  enum  Mono / Stereo Codes
            Sample  -->  Bit  (  Integer  )      //  Should  become  enum  Bit Codes  ,  should  get  Default  Value  Sixteen Bit
            Sample  -->  Sampling Rate  (  Long  )      //  Should  get  Default  Value  44100
            Sample  -->  Real Time Per Virtual Time  (  Double  )      //  Should  get  Default  Value  1
            Sample  -->  Interpolation  (  Integer  )      //  Should  become  enum  Wave Interpolation Types  with  Default  Value  Line Interpolation
            Sample  -->  Active  (  Boolean  )      //  Should  get  Default  Value  True
            Sample  -->  Amplifier  (  Double  )      //  Should  get  Default  Value  1
            Sample  -->  Bytes To Skip  (  Long  )
            Sample  -->  Time  (  Double  )
            Sample  -->  Value  (  Double  )

            Sample Sample  -->  Value  (  Integer  )

            Midi File  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Wave File Output  -->  Name  (  String  )
            Wave File Output  -->  Mono / Stereo  (  Integer  )      //  Should  become  Enum  Mono / Stereo Codes
            Wave File Output  -->  Bit  (  Integer  )      //  Should  become  Enum  Bit Codes,  with  Default  Value  Sixteen Bit
            Wave File Output  -->  Sampling Rate  (  Long  )      //  Should  get  Default  Value  44100
            Wave File Output  -->  File Path  (  String  )
            Wave File Output  -->  Start Time  (  Double  )      //  Should  get  Default  Value  0
            Wave File Output  -->  End Time  (  Double  )      //  Should  get  Default  Value  1
            Wave File Output  -->  Duration  (  Double  )      //  Should  become  derived  :  Duration  =  EndTime  -  StartTime
            Wave File Output  -->  Real Time Per Virtual Time  (  Double  )      //  Should  get  Default  Value  1
            Wave File Output  -->  Amplifier  (  Double  )      //  Should  get  Default  Value  1

            Midi File Output  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Wave In  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Wave Out  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Midi In  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Midi Out  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Scale  -->  Name  (  String  )
            Scale  -->  Constant Ordinals Per Octave  (  Boolean  )
            Scale  -->  Ordinals Per Octave  (  Long  )

            Scale Tone  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Octave  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Octave Ordinal  -->  Name  (  String  )
            Octave Ordinal  -->  Scale Tone Position  (  String  )

            Sequence  -->  Name  (  String  )

            Sequence Tone  -->  Start  (  Double  )
            Sequence Tone  -->  Length  (  Double  )
            Sequence Tone  -->  Primary Scale Reference  (  Integer  )      //  Should  become  an  enum
            Sequence Tone  -->  Scale Position  (  Long  )
            Sequence Tone  -->  Scale Octave  (  Long  )
            Sequence Tone  -->  Scale Ordinal  (  Long  )

